OL,3,AAberfan stops to remember 60 years
OL,4,Asince coal tip collapsed, killing 116
OL,5,Achildren and 28 adults
OL,6,
OL,7,FPeople in Aberfan, south Wales, are
OL,8,Fremembering the disaster 60 years ago
OL,9,Fwhen a coal waste tip collapsed on a
OL,10,Fschool and homes
OL,12,FA prayer and moment of silence was held
OL,13,Fat 09:15 to mark the moment, and a male
OL,14,Fvoice choir formed in the aftermath of
OL,15,Fthe disaster will sing
OL,17,FOn 21 October 1966, 116 children and 28
OL,18,Fadults were killed when the colliery
OL,19,Fspoil tip collapsed and engulfed
OL,20,FPantglas Junior School and surrounding
OL,21,Fhouses
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/3
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,0,100
